;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 by the user (written by Claude, from design
;; section 15, DCL Dictionary DCL1-5, the LIB$ and System Services
;; manuals, the guest runs and the debugger run). Why this is right:
;; - TEXT holds the arguments, each ended by 0X: 2050 bytes, room for
;;   argument 0 (at most 1024 bytes, POC_IMAGE_NAME's buffer) and the
;;   line (1024) split, each with its 0X. STARTS holds where each
;;   starts: 513 INTEGERs, as each argument after 0 takes a character
;;   and a blank but the last. ArgCount is exported, a global symbol
;;   ("::").
;; - The initializer calls Split. Split has POC_IMAGE_NAME put argument
;;   0 ($GETJPI's JPI$_IMAGNAME) in LINE, its length back in R0, and
;;   copies it to the start of TEXT with its 0X; ArgCount is 1. Then
;;   POC_FOREIGN puts LIB$GET_FOREIGN's line in LINE ("" when the image
;;   was not run as a foreign command).
;; - Split's loop skips blanks (32 and 9), stops at the line's end, and
;;   records where the next argument starts and counts it. Then, until a
;;   blank outside quotes or the end: a character other than " (34) is
;;   copied; "" inside quotes is copied as one "; any other " toggles
;;   quoted (XORB2 #1) and is dropped. Then the argument's 0X. Every
;;   index is checked against its array (trap 2), as poc's range checks
;;   always are.
;; - GetArg returns at once for an array of length 0; else it copies
;;   argument n, if 0 <= n < ArgCount (CMPW, words under -O2), from
;;   TEXT[STARTS[n]] up to its 0X or LEN(val) - 1 characters, and ends
;;   val with 0X, which makes val "" for any other n.
;; - On the guest, ArgsOut run as a foreign command with -o "Hello"
;;   mixedCase a"b"c "x""y" "" "two  spaces"<TAB>tab prints -O, Hello,
;;   MIXEDCASE, AbC, x"y, "", two  spaces and TAB, under -O2 and -OC;
;;   run by RUN, it has argument 0 alone (guest-run.expected).
;; - GetIntArg and ArgPos (2026-10-10, for the fixtures step 5 runs on
;;   the VAX, section 16, proposal 6), as rtl/llvm's: GetIntArg gets
;;   argument n into a 64-character array by GetArg, then reads an
;;   optional - and decimal digits, each index checked (trap 2), and
;;   stores the number in val only when a digit was read; ArgPos
;;   compares each argument with s, a copy of the open array made on
;;   entry, by POC_STRCMP, a new external, and returns the first that is
;;   equal, or ArgCount. The comment that grew moves the trap lines
;;   after it down one (PUSHL #48 for #47).
; Modules, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
